# Bally Star Trek (1979): what the playfield does on its own when a coil fires.
# The game fires the coil; the machine moves the ball or the targets, and these switches change.

# The outhole kicker serves the ball: it leaves the outhole
physics SOL_OUTHOLE opens SW_OUTHOLE
# The saucer kicks out its ball
physics SOL_SAUCER opens SW_SAUCER
# The drop target reset stands all four targets up
physics SOL_DROP_TARGET_RESET opens SW_DROP_1 SW_DROP_2 SW_DROP_3 SW_DROP_4

# Power on with the ball in the outhole
close SW_OUTHOLE
